# elohim-protocol/ — the protocol canon (governed)

This directory is the vision. Its governance base is the **sovereignty ontology guard** (bound from
`.claude/epr-meta/policies.yaml`, realized by `epr:validator-sovereignty-ontology-guard`): a write that
NET-NEW introduces apex-assertion sovereignty framing ("self-sovereign" as the top identity tier, "true
data sovereignty" as a goal) draws an `ask` that affirms the frame against the three legitimate uses
(adversary / bounded / bridge-legibility) and points at the canon. It is a **guard, not a ban** — one
keystroke to proceed when the usage is legitimate — and it fires only on *introduction*, so editing a
doc to *clean* its sovereignty framing is never trapped. Dismissals aggregate through
`sovereignty-guard-signal.py` (PostToolUse) into a drift ledger so the rule itself surfaces for
evaluation: the protocol exercising its own governance over the bytes of this repo.
